# Git identity — no Cursor contributor

When creating commits or preparing GitHub deploys for this repo:

- **Author must be the human user only** (local `git config user.name` / `user.email`). Never set author/committer to Cursor, Cursor Agent, or any `*cursor*` identity.
- **Never add** `Co-authored-by: Cursor`, `Co-authored-by: Cursor Agent`, or any Cursor-related trailer to commit messages.
- **Never** use `--author` with a Cursor name/email.
- Do not amend history to insert Cursor as author or co-author.
- If a commit tool or UI suggests adding Cursor as co-author, omit it.

Tab title / product copy is unrelated — this rule is only about git/GitHub attribution.
